l,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.0968606635804084,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.046978931545025526,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":20.654985754985756,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.05213,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":34.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"CRISPR Therapeutics AG, a gene editing company, focuses on developing gene-based medicines for serious human diseases using its Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short Palindromic Repeats (CRISPR)/CRISPR-associated protein 9 (Cas9) platform. The company's CRISPR/Cas9 is a technology for gene editing which is the process of precisely altering specific sequences of genomic DNA. It has a portfolio of therapeutic programs across a range of disease areas, including hemoglobinopathies, CAR T cell therapies, in vivo, and type 1 diabetes, as well as develops investigational CAR T programs, including an autologous, gene-edited CAR T program targeting allogeneic chimeric antigen receptor T cell for autoimmune indications and oncology. The company's lead product candidate is CASGEVY, an ex vivo CRISPR/Cas9 gene-edited cell therapy for treating patients suffering from transfusion-dependent beta-thalassemia, severe sickle cell disease (SCD), and hemoglobinopathies in which a patient's hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells are edited to produce high levels of fetal hemoglobin in red blood cells. It also develops CAR T cell therapies, including CTX112 targeting cluster of differentiation 19 (CD19) and CTX131 targeting CD70 for oncology and autoimmune indications; CTX310 and CTX320, in vivo gene editing to address the cardiovascular disease by disrupting the validated targets angiopoietin-like protein 3 and lipoprotein; and CTX211, an allogeneic, gene-edited, hypoimmune stem cell-derived product candidate for the treatment of T1D. It has strategic partnerships with Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated. CRISPR Therapeutics AG was incorporated in 2013 and is headquartered in Zug, Switzerland.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Samarth  Kulkarni Ph.D. | CEO & Chairman | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["CRISPR Therapeutics AG is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.1B market cap on $4M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +43% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -304% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $346M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 9.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 2065% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 18934% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 133% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"CRISPR Therapeutics (CRSP) Stock May Look Stretched As Fresh Gene Editing Data Lands","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-crsp/crispr-therapeutics/news/crispr-therapeutics-crsp-stock-may-look-stretched-as-fresh-g","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795623203.757,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is CRISPR Therapeutics (NASDAQ:CRSP) Quietly Strengthening Its Position?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/healthcare/is-crispr-therapeutics-nasdaqcrsp-quietly-strengthening-its-posi